NOTES: Three.js: PerspectiveCamera (fov ~35) with OrbitControls, target at (1.0, 1.0, 1.2) in world coords with Z-up (or Y-up with the scene rotated). Build the surface as a ParametricGeometry / PlaneGeometry (64×64) whose z is evaluated from the parsed expression; re-evaluate positions and recompute normals on equation change rather than rebuilding the mesh. Parse f with a small safe math parser (mathjs-style) supporting + - * / ^, sin, cos, exp, sqrt, abs; show parse errors inline under the field and keep the last valid surface. Region membership test: implicit blob function or point-in-polygon against a precomputed boundary polyline; use it both to clip grid lines (LineSegments filtered per-segment) and to decide which subrectangles get columns in 'All columns' mode. Render columns as a single InstancedMesh of unit boxes scaled per instance for performance at n=24. Use MeshBasicMaterial/MeshStandardMaterial with transparent:true, depthWrite:false and renderOrder so the translucent surface, cylinder wall and orange columns composite correctly; sort: plane → wall → columns → surface. Dashed line via LineDashedMaterial with computeLineDistances(). Drag the sample point by raycasting against an invisible plane at z=0, clamp the result to inside R, then snap the column base to the containing subrectangle while the red dot stays at the exact drag position. Labels and leader arrows as CSS2DRenderer HTML overlays with KaTeX, anchored to 3D anchor points so they track the camera. Live numeric readout panel: x*_k, y*_k, f(x*_k,y*_k), ΔA_k, f·ΔA_k, and (in all-columns mode) the running Riemann sum Σ f(x*_k,y*_k)ΔA_k.

